From 8cc73319c2eeff2d816396d85514d31000d0359b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 12:12:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make Blue Chats production-ready: real SMS auth, Bunny
 uploads, live WebRTC calls

Replaces the mock/local-only data layer with real Firebase and fixes
security issues found while auditing the app.

Security fixes
- Remove Bunny storage password hardcoded in server.ts (rotate it: it is
  still in git history)
- Close CEO auth bypass: POSTing a designated email to
  /api/admin/verify-claims granted admin without any token. Admin access
  now requires a verified Firebase ID token plus a server-assigned claim
- Firestore rules rewritten: chats/messages/calls readable only by
  participants; no impersonation; phone numbers claimable only by their
  verified owner; admin data requires the ceo claim (12 rules tests)
- Uploads require sign-in, are type/size validated, get unguessable
  server-generated paths, and can only be deleted by their owner

New features
- Firebase Phone Auth with real SMS codes (invisible reCAPTCHA, 6-digit
  code, resend cooldown, clear error messages)
- Bunny.net media: authenticated upload proxy with progress, region/CDN
  support, streaming proxy with Range, delete + CDN purge, live self-test
- Live WebRTC voice/video calls using Firestore signalling: ringing,
  accept/decline/busy/missed, mute, camera toggle/switch, recording with
  notice to the other party, TURN support (static, coturn, Cloudflare)
- Branding config + runtime accent colours, persisted dark mode, i18n

Broken features fixed
- Firebase API key in code was invalid, so nothing was ever saved; config
  is now loaded at runtime from env with a setup screen when missing
- Real-time chats, groups, read receipts, typing, reactions, replies
- Contacts by phone, status stories (24h), Discover, friend requests,
  wallet pre-registration and CEO dashboard all persist in Firestore
- In-app dark mode toggle had no effect (Tailwind v4 media variant)
- Failed uploads reported success and sent blob: URLs
- iOS voice notes (hardcoded audio/webm), black camera preview
- Logged-out users never saw sign-in; production `npm start` crashed

Verified with a two-browser E2E test (25 steps) against the Firebase
emulators and a mock Bunny server.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
